Yes — in a production pipeline, Scout’s output should be shaped so it can be fed directly into Cook Ding (or into a trivial “handoff reducer” that does no reasoning).


Right now the Scout output is a whole-ox evidence world plus maps. Cook Ding doesn’t need all of that. Cook Ding needs one thing:


an Evidence Pack: primary text excerpts + metadata + locations + hashes.


So the clean architecture is:


Scout returns (1) Whole Ox and (2) Cook Ding Pack in the same JSON.

Cook Ding consumes only cook_ding_input.

Everything else is for observability/debugging.


